# E3: the TP4 G1 reference (the S3 matrix plan of the S2 window, at its 4k and 16k users). The same matrix plan, the same four
# prompts (512 / 1,536 / 4,096 / 16,384: the user index and the length fix the prompt) and 256 tokens out on general-tp4 (the
# general path: no fast path, the device sampler). Its solo texts are what E1's solo texts are compared with, offline, per user:
# where the first divergence falls. Bit equality is not expected (another engine and reduction order); a first divergence at a
# near-tie after a long agreeing prefix is the pass reading, one before token 10 or a gibberish fast-path text is a defect. The 4,096
# and 16,384 users are the ones the S2 window's matrix compared; the 512 and 1,536 users are read the same way and exist to keep
# the prompts aligned with E1's.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the four-card speed window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/speed and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here
# names a rig, a card or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG names the image K0 builds from this same commit; a later commit needs a new tag.
# Duration (estimate): reset 1-3 min; per arm an engine build 3-8 min plus 3-8 min of streams: 15 / 25 / 50 min.
# SOFT: a verdict other than PASS here does not stop the window, the texts are the product.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset gate
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-speed-1
C2_PROFILE=general-tp4
C2_GATE_PLAN=matrix
C2_GATE_LENGTHS=512,1536,4096,16384
C2_GATE_MAX_TOKENS=256
